WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.310 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  tonight we are learning a bit more about  the victims killed in that  tragic highway crash on thursday thank  you for joining us  at six i'm brian loftis and i'm kirsten  joyce  the victims come from a tight-knit  cycling community which is still of  course  reeling from this tragedy their names  released by the clark county coroner's  office tonight they include  39 year old aaron ray 57 year old  michael murray  48 year old eskoy ahmet 57 year old  thomas  traeger and 41-year-old gerard nieva  the crash happened thursday morning in  between boulder city and searchlight  when a box truck collided with the group  of cyclists and their support vehicle on  the freeway  a news now reporter madison kimbrell on  this story live from  university medical center with how the  community is coming together  following this tragedy  yeah one of the cyclists injured was  airlifted here to umc  trauma in trauma in critical condition  now cyclists all around the community  here in las vegas are really rallying  together  to do as much as they can to help as  much as they can  take a look at the video that we shot  where you can see the extent of the  scene  four men and one woman died yesterday  after a box truck that was driving in  the same direction  as the group of cyclists veered into  their lane killing and injuring several  riders this happened on u.s 95 south of  boulder highway at mile marker 35.  as of now we know that three people are  injured but we don't know the status  at this time two were transported  immediately to the hospital  that's according to the nhp trooper that  was on scene  the other person injured did not seem to  have life-threatening injuries  fellow cyclist friend and former metro  police officer michael anderson was  there yesterday  and shared some words we do this nipton  loop every year  no problems  this year we just  just in the wrong places a long time  anderson created this gofundme page for  his friends and on it he lists the names  of the cyclists who lost their lives  along with those that are still fighting  he says the main purpose of the gofundme  page is to ease some of the financial  strain the families may be going through  right now  if you are interested in contributing to  that gofundme page we have a link  up on our website of course we'll keep  you updated on this story  as more information comes through  reporting live from umc  madison kimbrough 8 news now

